WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:06.000
[Music]

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.699
As you walk into the Knight Management Center and you look

00:00:08.699 --> 00:00:11.949
to the left, you will notice the cornerstone of the center

00:00:11.969 --> 00:00:15.820
with an inscription that reads "Dedicated to the things that

00:00:15.839 --> 00:00:18.989
haven't happened yet and the people who are going to dream

00:00:19.009 --> 00:00:21.949
them up". And I love that inscription because to me it so

00:00:21.949 --> 00:00:25.750
completely captures the essence of what the GSB is about

00:00:25.769 --> 00:00:29.460
which after all is innovation and it speaks to our twofold

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:33.949
mission. On the one hand it is the creation of the ideas by

00:00:33.969 --> 00:00:38.049
the faculty in a great research university which will inform

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:42.249
the practice of management. On the other hand that portal is

00:00:42.269 --> 00:00:45.379
a portal to generations of students who will enter the

00:00:45.399 --> 00:00:50.019
complex and begin a process of personal transformation, a

00:00:50.039 --> 00:00:53.909
process that will enable them to dream up those things that

00:00:53.929 --> 00:00:58.069
haven't happened yet, and through that, to change lives,

00:00:58.089 --> 00:01:01.509
change organizations and change the world.

00:01:01.529 --> 00:01:04.260
In the curriculum we start with other core perspectives, we

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:07.560
deal with issues like ethics, strategic leadership and the

00:01:07.579 --> 00:01:10.870
global context of management. These are the core concepts

00:01:10.890 --> 00:01:13.609
that a leader who is looking at how to take their

00:01:13.609 --> 00:01:17.340
organization forward has to be familiar with. We also then

00:01:17.359 --> 00:01:20.590
do a deep dive into every core foundation. This is the

00:01:20.609 --> 00:01:24.209
nitty-gritty of the basic management skills and knowledge

00:01:24.229 --> 00:01:26.750
that any leader of the management organization has to

00:01:26.769 --> 00:01:30.439
master. We are talking about finance, operations, marketing

00:01:30.459 --> 00:01:33.790
and so on. But to really change the world, you have to know

00:01:33.810 --> 00:01:37.370
how to lead and we think that that involves three essential

00:01:37.390 --> 00:01:40.019
capabilities. Firstly, you need to be able to understand

00:01:40.039 --> 00:01:42.929
what the problem is. So that's where critical analytical

00:01:42.949 --> 00:01:45.870
thinking comes in. Then you need to think about what the

00:01:45.890 --> 00:01:48.739
solution is. Well that's where innovation comes in. Finally,

00:01:48.759 --> 00:01:52.009
you have to be able to take that and implement it, and that'

00:01:52.009 --> 00:01:54.259
s where personal leadership comes into effect. Our approach

00:01:54.259 --> 00:01:56.509
to critical analytical thinking is pretty unique. We start

00:01:56.509 --> 00:01:59.149
with a very intimate seminar in the full quarter. In that

00:01:59.149 --> 00:02:01.399
seminar, we look at some pretty interesting issues for

00:02:01.399 --> 00:02:04.169
example, what should Google do in China and we look at the

00:02:04.169 --> 00:02:07.329
HP's decision around Mark Hurd's resignation. But what we

00:02:07.349 --> 00:02:11.009
are really doing beyond our focus on the issues is teaching

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:13.009
our students about argumentation.

00:02:13.030 --> 00:02:16.239
Personal leadership starts with self-awareness and then it

00:02:16.259 --> 00:02:19.509
is about how you interact with others. There are couples of

00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:21.780
things that are distinctive and unique about our approach.

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:25.030
One builds on the long legacy of the GSB which is of course

00:02:25.030 --> 00:02:27.280
interpersonal dynamics known to many as touchy feeling. The

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:30.789
other is coaching, helping them to learn through skills

00:02:30.810 --> 00:02:34.449
based exercises how to be effective leaders. The third

00:02:34.469 --> 00:02:37.319
capability is innovative thinking. Here, we are moving

00:02:37.340 --> 00:02:40.389
aggressively to try to incorporate some of the learnings we

00:02:40.409 --> 00:02:42.879
have gotten from working with the design school around

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:45.589
innovation. An example of the kind of collaborative work

00:02:45.609 --> 00:02:48.159
that we have done there is Jim Patell's course on

00:02:48.159 --> 00:02:50.979
Entrepreneurial Design for Extreme Affordability. We are

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:53.829
tremendously excited that this personal transformation is

00:02:53.849 --> 00:02:56.599
going to have a new home in the Knight Management Center

00:02:56.599 --> 00:02:59.099
which opens in this spring. The Knight Management Center has

00:02:59.099 --> 00:03:02.109
8 buildings arranged around three plots with a wide variety

00:03:02.129 --> 00:03:05.019
of space that's quite different from what we have now. More

00:03:05.019 --> 00:03:09.139
flat classrooms, more breakout rooms and we are going to

00:03:09.159 --> 00:03:11.909
have a co-lab which is a garage like space where the

00:03:11.909 --> 00:03:14.909
students are going to be able to roll up their sleeves and

00:03:14.909 --> 00:03:17.919
do innovative new projects in an actual hands-on way. We

00:03:17.939 --> 00:03:20.709
envision a space that is very collaborative, a space where

00:03:20.729 --> 00:03:23.169
students get together around a table to dream up the next

00:03:23.169 --> 00:03:26.319
business plan the way Phil Knight did while he was at the

00:03:26.340 --> 00:03:30.339
business school. It is really a home for innovation. As the

00:03:30.359 --> 00:03:33.039
Knight Management Center approaches completion, I really

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:35.599
want to thank you for all of your contributions, great and

00:03:35.599 --> 00:03:38.549
small which have made this possible and I look forward to

00:03:38.569 --> 00:03:40.579
your continued participation in the life of the school

00:03:40.579 --> 00:03:44.999
whether it's as the mentor, as a volunteer, coming back for

00:03:45.019 --> 00:03:49.049
your reunion or as a donor. Thank you so much for being part

00:03:49.069 --> 00:03:51.659
of the life of the school and for everything that you do for

00:03:51.659 --> 00:03:54.999
us. If you really want to see the impact on our students,

00:03:55.019 --> 00:03:58.019
please click on the link on the page, we have got recent

00:03:58.019 --> 00:04:00.269
quotes from our students who describe their own personal

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.000
transformation.

